{"name":"Warm Asphalt","hex":"#9c9395","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a somewhat high temperature, often but not always connoting that the high temperature is pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","Friendly and with affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep warm.","To become warm, to heat up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm"},{"term":"asphalt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sticky, black to brown and highly viscous liquid or semi-solid, composed almost entirely of bitumen with small mineral particles, that is present in most crude petroleums and in some natural deposits.","Ellipsis of asphalt concrete, a hard ground covering used for roads and walkways."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pave with asphalt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asphalt"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"warm":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg/En-us-warm.ogg.mp3"}],"asphalt":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/En-us-asphalt.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a8/En-us-asphalt.ogg/En-us-asphalt.ogg.mp3"}]}}}